# Without this, `COPY . .` in Dockerfile.prod's builder stage copies the
# HOST's own node_modules (2.9GB, confirmed via a real build — "Sending
# build context to Docker daemon 2.9GB") right on top of the one `npm ci`
# just installed inside the container. That's wasteful on its own, but the
# real bug it caused: this repo's own node_modules/.bin/next has no execute
# bit (-rw-rw-r--, confirmed) since every local command in this project
# invokes `node node_modules/next/dist/bin/next` directly rather than the
# `next` shell wrapper — once copied into the image, `npm run build`'s
# `next build` (which DOES exec that wrapper) failed with a flat
# "Permission denied". Same class of bug the dev Dockerfile/compose never
# hit, only because dev compose bind-mounts the real source directory over
# the image afterward anyway, silently masking it.
node_modules
.next
.git
*.md
.env*
